  <!-- 11. AppleCare & insurance -->
  <section class="pb-section" id="applecare-insurance">
    <h2>Does AppleCare+, warranty or insurance cover water damage?</h2>
    <p class="lead-in"><strong>Apple's warranty: no. AppleCare+: yes, for a A$429 fee. Home insurance: only if you have accidental damage cover.</strong></p>
    <div class="cover-grid">
      <div class="cover-card no"><h3>Apple's 1-year warranty</h3><p><strong>Not covered.</strong> Apple says liquid damage to Macs is not covered by its warranty. Mac laptops have liquid contact indicators inside that show it.</p><p class="source"><a href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/102249" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Apple Support</a></p></div>
      <div class="cover-card yes"><h3>AppleCare+</h3><p><strong>Covered</strong> as accidental damage. Apple's Australian estimate for MacBook Air and Pro "other accidental damage" is <strong>A$429</strong>. If you have it, Apple is often the cheaper choice. Get your files out first if you have no backup.</p><p class="source"><a href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/mac-laptops/repair?services=applecare" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Apple repair estimator</a></p></div>
      <div class="cover-card maybe"><h3>Home contents insurance</h3><p><strong>Maybe.</strong> Many policies only cover a spill if you added accidental damage cover. Outside the home you usually need portable items cover. Check your policy wording.</p><p class="source"><a href="https://www.racv.com.au/royalauto/property/insurance/insurance-for-laptops-guide.html" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">RACV example</a></p></div>
    </div>
    <h3>Making an insurance claim? Our report costs $149</h3>
    <ul class="check-list">
      <li>What happened and what we found inside</li>
      <li>Which parts are damaged, with photos</li>
      <li>The cost to repair, or why it is not worth repairing</li>
      <li>Your Mac's model and serial number</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

